   "gap": "Supply the full treatment of the source's Section 11 claims attached to the original equations: Huber states (p.96) that Proposals 1 and 2 are asymptotically minimax when k is chosen in relation to the true epsilon, and (p.96) that Proposal 2's S is more accurate than Proposal 1's (log S having the smaller asymptotic variance). The handbook proves Proposal 2's matched-k minimax value but only the population worst case of Proposal 1, and states explicitly (071 body lines 288-294 and 303-312) that Proposal 1's sampling-level asymptotic minimaxity (consistency of T_n and limiting truncated risk V_1(F) for the integer-valued second equation under a specified boundary convention and target integer) and the Proposal 2 versus Proposal 1 asymptotic scale-variance comparison are not established. Prove these, or prove their exact qualified form or a counterexample, in the owned files.",
